Rit licensing
=============

The repository owner offers copyright-controlled, independently authored Rit
contributions under either of these licenses, at the recipient's option:

  * MIT, in LICENSE-MIT
  * Apache License, Version 2.0, in LICENSE-APACHE

SPDX expression for that contribution grant: MIT OR Apache-2.0.

This grant does not withdraw licenses already granted. It does not claim
ownership of third-party material or grant rights the owner does not hold.
Copied, translated, imported, or otherwise derived third-party material keeps
its original terms, even when a file also contains original Rit contributions.

Third-party and inherited material
----------------------------------

  * vendor/sley retains Apache-2.0, including local adaptations.
  * Connected upstream Git at compat/git retains its own source notices and
    COPYING. Git's COPYING selects GPL version 2 unless otherwise stated.
  * Inherited Git documentation, fixtures and notices retain their Git terms.
  * External dependencies retain their own grants and required notices.

No root license or package metadata overrides those terms. The project
contribution grant excludes vendor/, compat/git, inherited Git material and
third-party dependency code except where an explicit grant already applies.
Future imports must retain their actual licenses and source provenance.

Native and compatibility executables
------------------------------------

The native Rit executable links the Apache-2.0 Sley Rust engine and frontend.
Rit-controlled entrypoint contributions remain MIT OR Apache-2.0. Preserve
Sley's Apache-2.0 notice and all applicable dependency notices when distributing
that executable.

The connected Git compatibility executable is built and executed separately.
Its source and distribution remain subject to Git's applicable license terms.
Separate process execution does not remove obligations to retain notices or
supply corresponding source when those terms require it. The complete source
repository and compatibility distribution are not uniformly permissive.

See Documentation/gitr/licensing.md and vendor/sley/NOTICE.md. Keep LICENSE,
LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE, COPYING and applicable donor notices with source
distributions.
